# FIVE 共享案例目录与阶段交接契约

## Gold-standard authority and layout

[Examples index](../../../../examples/README.md), [sum3](../../../../examples/models/sum3/README.md), [sum2](../../../../examples/models/sum2/README.md), and [cross-model relations](../../../../examples/relations/) are the normative, maintained artifact examples for all future FIVE verification work. Read the relevant concrete reference before creating artifacts. Their format is authoritative; their particular inputs, preconditions and outcomes do not constrain another user's problem.

The outer case location is project-selected. Its internal C workflow has exactly four stage output directories, in dependency order:

```text
<case>/
  prepare/{source/,report/,handoff.json}
  cbmc/{harness.c,report/,handoff.json}   # actual harness/log filenames follow the examples
  align/{model/,report/,handoff.json}   # generated declarations remain model artifacts
  rocq/{support/,report/,handoff.json,spec-recheck.json}
    no_error/{problem/,attempts/001/}
    termination/{problem/,attempts/001/}
    cbmc_recheck/{problem/,attempts/001/}
<examples-or-project>/relations/<relation>/{problem/,attempts/001/}
```

Each stage has `report/report.md`, `report/costs.json` and `handoff.json`; the handoff binds input/output roles, paths and SHA-256. Preserve tool manifests where actually produced. Paths below such as `source/`, `model/` and generated `proof/` are relative to their owning stage: prepared source is `prepare/source/`, generated AST is `align/model/Source.v`, and generated obligation scaffolding is `align/model/proof/`. Actual proofs belong under `rocq/<problem>/attempts/`, never in place of the immutable generated model. Shared evidence may live elsewhere if a resolvable hash-bound reference identifies it.

For a complete C workflow, freeze source, dependencies, verification request, requested properties/conditions/bounds and target before checking; preserve every actual emitted property ID in the CBMC handoff before mapping. `prepare/handoff.json` is CBMC input; `cbmc/handoff.json` is align input; `align/handoff.json` is Rocq input. Each next stage verifies status and hashes of all transitive artifacts it consumes. The prepared C and bindings are identical throughout. Missing request/input or changed hashes block dependent work instead of silently substituting inputs. Pure model generation and pure Rocq requests run only the applicable stages; record others `not_run` or `not_applicable`, without fabricating source, CBMC runs or proofs. Standalone align may generate a model without CBMC, recording mapping as not applicable.

Status describes evidence: `not_run`, `not_applicable`, `blocked`, `pending`, `failed`, `proved` or `refuted` as applicable. A generation stage can finish with explicitly pending proofs when generation alone was requested. A real counterexample with checked replay can complete a requested refutation; this is never program correctness. Do not claim whole-task `COMPLETE` while any requested goal, actual CBMC property ID or required independent receipt remains open. Report the actual result and remaining items; unobserved cost figures are `null`, with reasons, and observed figures are `recorded`. Do not label a user-facing result summary `partial`; raw telemetry status is preserved unchanged.

## 固定交接接口

每个阶段读取当前 case 中前序阶段的 handoff 与自身阶段的 `report/report.md`、`report/costs.json`（首次调用时建立），在启动前核对直接输入的路径、hash、目标配置和前一阶段状态；有缺失、内容变化或依赖不可用时停止依赖该输入的步骤，登记原因，不静默替代。执行完成后仅增量更新自己的阶段状态、输入/输出路径与 SHA-256、工具版本/选项和成本引用。路径均以 case 目录为基准，允许指向存在的共享文件。状态只能表示实际证据支持的程度。报告生成/类型检查、证明、成本审核分别记状态。

| skill | 必需输入 | 写入与交给下游 |
|---|---|---|
| five-prepare | 原 C、入口、目标语义、依赖及用户要求；输入可来自案例外 | `prepare/source/<entry>.c`、实际依赖和 `prepare/source/bindings.json`；在报告/handoff 固定准备结果和限制，供 CBMC 与 align 消费 |
| five-cbmc | 已准备的 `prepare/source/`、bindings、入口和用户指定检查性质/界限 | `cbmc/` 的 harness、命令、属性、假设、范围、结果及实际反例，handoff 索引并标明状态；交给 align |
| five-align | 已准备的 `prepare/source/` 和 bindings；若映射 CBMC 规约，还需实际 `cbmc/` 属性与范围 | `align/model/preprocessed.i`、`align/model/Source.v`、`align/model/Execution.v`、生成的三个 `align/model/proof/*.v`、来源审计及适用时由 handoff 的 spec-map 角色绑定的属性映射，供 rocq 使用；未运行 CBMC 不阻塞模型生成 |
| five-rocq | 一个或多个已有 Rocq 模型及用户目标；CompCert 任务还读 align 的模型、义务和映射 | 前条件、规约、证明和假设、内核证据及适用时 `rocq/spec-recheck.json`，交给 verify；纯 Rocq 无需 C 或 CBMC |
| five-verify | 用户目标和案例清单；分别读取所请求阶段的实际交付 | 调度与接口检查，引用四阶段 `report/` 并更新案例汇总（不新增第五个阶段目录）、未完成项及去重后的成本；不将生成当证明 |

`prepare/source/bindings.json` 至少登记：原始源文件与准备后的源文件路径及 SHA-256、实际依赖与版本或 hash、入口、C 方言和目标 ABI/端序/浮点与舍入、预处理和编译选项、外部调用原绑定与实际绑定、重定向实现及其来源/哈希、尚需证明的对应关系。未知或不可恢复字段写 `null` 并说明原因；不得猜测未发生重定向。准备后的程序是两个分支的相同输入；改回原库绑定的性质迁移必须另有对应性证据。

每个实际阶段在 `<stage>/handoff.json` 使用 `schema: "five-stage-handoff/1"`，包含 `case_id`、`stage`、`status`、`target`、`paths_relative_to`、`outputs`、`limitations` 及适用的 `next_stage`。`outputs` 每项含 `role`、case 相对 `path` 和小写 SHA-256 `sha256`，包括供下游使用的传递输入。阶段报告和成本分别为 `<stage>/report/report.md`、`<stage>/report/costs.json`。补充 manifest 仅在实际工具或案例使用时保留并 hash 绑定，不要求案例根目录另建 `report/` 或虚构第五个阶段目录。先读取真实 handoff 的 role/path 再解析文件，不从历史默认文件名猜输入。生成的 CompCert manifest 保持工具原 schema，不能改成 handoff schema。

未知数值为 `null` 和原因，不能用 0 或估算。失败、重试及准备阶段均计入；案例独立边界需在开始前采集，批次共享消耗单列并引用，不能伪造逐案例实测或重复相加。每个实际执行阶段通过 `scripts/audit-costs.py --run RUN_DIR` 核查计量证据；审计完整性与验证结果独立陈述。

`report/costs.json` 使用 `schema: "five-stage-costs/1"`，以 `records` 数组保存本阶段及适用的历史或共享记录。每条记录有 `stage`、`run`、`status`、`evidence` 和三组实测字段：

- `time.wall_seconds`、`time.tool_cpu_seconds`
- `token.input`、`token.output`、`token.total`、`token.cached_input`、`token.reasoning_output`
- `memory.tool_peak_rss_bytes`（采样峰值）

保留计量范围及证据引用；无观测的字段为 `null`。缓存和推理 token 分别是输入和输出的子集。原始 `metrics.json` 保留工具生成的格式。共享成本使用同一份证据，避免重复归属。

工具可能先把 CompCert 产物写入自身输出目录；align 必须保留原始导出/审计证据，再将经核对的预处理输入、原始 AST、执行包装和目标安装到上述案例路径，记录源路径及 hash。不能假定原工具默认输出路径已经符合共享接口。

## Problem and attempt contract

Each named problem has one canonical question in `problem/Spec.v`, `problem/report.md`, and `problem/status.json`. The report states the exact proposition, quantifiers, entry, preconditions, observation semantics, requested goals and pending goals. `status.json` uses `schema: "five-proof-problem/1"`, `status`, `active_attempt` (relative to `problem/`), `specification: "Spec.v"`, and `requested_goals`; it points explicitly to the current attempt. Additional helper modules may be imported by this canonical question; they do not replace it. Each attempt binds its actual checked specification snapshot and hash, so later canonical-question extension cannot retroactively change a historical claim. Cross-model problems use the same contract under `relations/<name>/` and bind every participating model.

Each real attempt uses a fresh numbered `attempts/<number>/` containing `Proof.v`, `check.py`, `report.md`, `costs.json`, and the referenced evidence. Its readable report records:

- exact target, conditions and specification version; what was proved/refuted and what remains pending;
- model identity, source/model/specification hashes, actual imports, entry/ABI/endianness/float and byte-observation semantics, external bindings, tool versions and inherited assumptions;
- actual LLM model, requested and observed reasoning effort, with runtime receipt (unknown observations remain `null`);
- commands and successful independent kernel-check receipts for claimed theorems, dependency/statement snapshots, assumptions output and reproducible checker;
- measured time, tokens and tool memory, measurement boundaries, raw receipts and shared-cost references.

All new reference proof workers use actual `gpt-6.1-sol` with `medium` reasoning effort, evidenced by runtime metadata; do not relabel a differently configured historical run. Keep historical actual attempts, including failures, immutable and visible. A new active attempt does not erase their cost or evidence; a failed superseded attempt does not make a now-proved current goal pending. Add clarification outside the historical attempt when necessary.

`costs.json` uses `five-stage-costs/1` and the `time`, `token`, `memory` groups above. Start a real CLI `--session` skill-session boundary before substantive work, finish that run on every outcome, and retain audit evidence. Count shared event IDs once. Per-attempt unobserved allocation is `null` plus a link to the shared record, never an invented split. Preserve raw telemetry; normalize measured figures in the report with scope, not by rewriting raw statuses.

Safety quantifies all reachable original Csem states; termination covers all possible successors (for example `Acc`), never merely bounded execution or an existing return path. Byte observations must state representation/endian, `Mem.loadbytes`/`memval` interpretation, output/write-prefix and frame scope; unknown bytes stay unknown. Generated models, compiled declarations and matching function names are not proofs. See [proof evidence](proof-evidence.md) for actual CBMC coverage and independent receipt requirements.

Closed active reference attempts additionally retain `evidence/goal-validation.json` (`five-proof-validation/1`). It binds the original input index, all current consumed sources, the exact compiled source snapshots and canonical kernel receipts. Exhaustive `goal_bindings` associate each requested goal with a fully qualified theorem and its expected Rocq type. A deterministic `GoalBinding.v` instantiates those types with the claimed theorems; retain its actual successful compilation, `Print Assumptions` output and independent kernel check. A nonempty goal list or an unrelated successful kernel command is insufficient. Reference full-compilation receipts allow load-path options (`-Q`, `-R`, `-I`), harmless `-q`/`-quiet`/`-time`, and exactly one `.v` source; output/module overrides, quick/skip/help modes and unsupported options fail closed. The validator supports the published unversioned `inputs` (repository-relative), unversioned `artifacts` (attempt-relative), `five-proof-attempt-provenance/1.files`, `five-proof-provenance/1.inputs` (case-relative) plus `shared_inputs` (repository-relative), and `five-proof-inputs/1.dependency_sha256` (repository-relative, with pinned external semantic hashes) indexes explicitly; missing, malformed or unknown layouts fail. Historical input/configuration receipts stay immutable; fresh current bindings govern the active verification.

Run `python3 scripts/check-example-artifacts.py` for reference metadata validation; `--compile` additionally reruns only active proof checkers. This complements semantic review and kernel checking; metadata validation cannot prove proposition adequacy.
# Rocq 证明证据与最终验收

five-align 交付模型、来源审计、spec-map 与待证目标；本文件规定 five-rocq 产出的证明证据以及 five-verify 的验收要求。模型生成阶段不要求这些定理已完成。

## 全执行对应证据

`execution-contract.json` 使用既有八类全执行义务。声明和对应关系由 align 交接；证明由 rocq 完成。最终声称全域执行对应时，每条必须 proof-backed、status proved，域与冻结 request 一致且 domain_restrictions 为空：

```text
execution_backend: compcert-csyntax-cexec
backend_manifest_sha256: 当前 manifest hash
alignment_issues: [{issue_id: 稳定ID, status: resolved, ...}]
```

execution_entry 绑定生成的 Execution.v/module/entry；source_semantics.source_sha256 至少包含原 C、Source.v 和 Execution.v，以及所用库适配器/规约/注册表。清楚列出可信外部库假设、world/volatile/I/O 范围。主 agent 审查命题充分性，metadata 本身不能证明命题覆盖完整。

无真实问题时 alignment_issues 为空；最终验收时实际问题须关闭。移交给 rocq 的待证义务不在生成阶段虚报为已解决。

## CBMC 独立重验结果

align 的 `spec-map.json` 是属性映射；rocq 在实际证明或反驳后输出 `spec-recheck.json`，schema 为 `five-cbmc-rocq-recheck/1`：

- request_sha256、backend_manifest_sha256 绑定同一请求和模型。
- verification_method 为 traditional-bounded-model-checking。
- cbmc_run、cbmc_command_id、cbmc_json 指向真实 CBMC 命令和原始 JSON stdout；cbmc_input_sha256 覆盖实际原 C/harness 等输入。
- properties 覆盖全部实际 property ID，不漏项、不重复。scope 保留原前条件、位置、内存区域、调用/展开范围和观察；theorem 是模型侧真实命题，evidence 是证明记录。
- 只有独立证据成立时才标 proved/refuted。现有完整重验门禁要求 SUCCESS 对应 proved、FAILURE 对应 refuted；UNKNOWN、超时、未完成或语义差异只能记 pending/gap，不能进入完整通过状态。
- 实际 FAILURE 的 counterexample_replay 绑定原始 trace、输入位/字节、出错操作和修改前缀。可用 Csem 执行关系证明复现，不要求直接 vm_compute。未复现不伪造 reproduced。反例证实表示原属性不成立。

CBMC 结论不是 Rocq 的公理，也不能以纯功能模型的相似断言代替执行层重验。

## 内核与假设证据

每个 evidence 的 kind 为 rocq-kernel-check，含 run、command_id、theorems、statement_artifacts、dependency_sha256。引用的 run.json 必须包含成功的实际 `rocq check`/`coqchk` 命令，检查所声称定理所在模块；禁止 admit/norec 等绕过检查选项。

依赖和声明应匹配真实 proof run 的输入快照，且在该运行中实际编译，不能只重填当前 hash。记录 `Print Assumptions` 和继承假设；声明编译通过并不证明待证命题。执行对应和属性重验使用相同证据标准。

## 最终门禁

```sh
python3 scripts/compcert-verify.py gate --request request.json \
  --request-sha256 FROZEN_HASH --contract execution-contract.json \
  --manifest _build/compcert/case/compcert-manifest.json \
  --spec-recheck spec-recheck.json
```

门禁实施新鲜来源审计、外部支持清单检查、全执行对应证明记录检查、实际 CBMC 属性的 Rocq 重验及问题关闭核查。不要求 agent 审批。最终验证统一使用 `compcert-verify.py gate`，不作为 align 的生成阶段验收条件。

门禁接受的范围是执行层与 CBMC 重验；独立的无错误、终止性和高层功能目标应另外核对相应 Rocq 定理的量词、前条件、实际证明/内核证据和当前依赖。不能因为 gate accepted 就把这些目标自动标为 proved。没有完整证据时给出范围明确的阶段报告和 pending 项。

## Gold-standard completion and observation boundary

The [shared case contract](case-contract.md) and its examples index define the normative problem/attempt layout. Validate the active attempt, preserving historical attempts and their original outcomes. A whole-task `COMPLETE` requires closure of every requested goal and every actual CBMC property ID under its original conditions, plus successful independent receipts bound to the exact current statements and dependencies. Checking one replacement assertion or a selected subset cannot close the original ledger. Counterexample replay may close an actual failed property as `refuted`, never as program correctness; unexplained UNKNOWN or semantic mismatch stays pending/gap. Generation-only requests correctly stop with declared pending obligations.

Memory-property statements must identify target representation and endian, source/destination ranges, CompCert `memval`/`Mem.loadbytes` interpretation, actual write prefix, and frame conditions. A numerical equality alone does not establish byte-copy or assertion-expression properties. All-reachable-state safety and all-successor termination remain distinct from finite executions or existence of a normal return. Metadata and a successful gate do not replace review of those quantifiers or additional requested goals.
"""Strict current proof receipt validation; historical attempts remain immutable."""
import hashlib
import json
from pathlib import Path
import re


def digest(path):
    return hashlib.sha256(Path(path).read_bytes()).hexdigest()


def certificate_source(imports, bindings):
    return ''.join(f'Require Import {name}.\n' for name in imports) + ''.join(
        f'Definition goal_{i} : {row["type"]} := {row["theorem"]}.\nPrint Assumptions goal_{i}.\n'
        for i, row in enumerate(bindings))


def input_index(root, active):
    """Explicit adapters for retained index formats, never a default empty list."""
    choices = [p for p in (active / 'inputs.json', active / 'provenance.json') if p.is_file()]
    if len(choices) != 1:
        raise ValueError('exactly one input index is required: ' + str(active))
    path = choices[0]
    data = json.loads(path.read_text())
    schema = data.get('schema')
    if schema == 'five-proof-attempt-provenance/1':
        groups = [(root, data.get('files'))]
    elif schema == 'five-proof-provenance/1':
        stages = [p for p in active.parents if p.name == 'rocq']
        if len(stages) != 1 or not data.get('model_configuration'):
            raise ValueError('invalid case provenance context: ' + str(path))
        groups = [(stages[0].parent, data.get('inputs')), (root, data.get('shared_inputs'))]
    elif schema == 'five-proof-inputs/1':
        hashes = data.get('dependency_sha256')
        semantics = data.get('semantic_dependencies')
        if not isinstance(hashes, dict) or not hashes or not isinstance(semantics, dict) or not semantics:
            raise ValueError('missing dependency/semantic hash maps: ' + str(path))
        for name, value in semantics.items():
            source = Path(name)
            if not source.is_absolute() or not source.is_file() or digest(source) != value:
                raise ValueError('stale external semantic dependency: ' + str(source))
        groups = [(root, [{'path': name, 'sha256': value} for name, value in hashes.items()])]
    elif path.name == 'inputs.json' and schema is None:
        # The two published pre-versioned layouts have distinct path bases.
        keys = [key for key in ('inputs', 'artifacts') if key in data]
        if len(keys) != 1:
            raise ValueError('ambiguous/missing legacy input rows: ' + str(path))
        key = keys[0]
        groups = [(active if key == 'artifacts' else root, data.get(key))]
    else:
        raise ValueError('unsupported input index schema: ' + str(path))
    rows = []
    for base, entries in groups:
        if not isinstance(entries, list) or not entries:
            raise ValueError('empty/malformed input index: ' + str(path))
        rows.extend((base, row) for row in entries)
    resolved = {}
    for base, row in rows:
        if not isinstance(row, dict) or not isinstance(row.get('path'), str) or not row['path'] or not re.fullmatch('[0-9a-f]{64}', str(row.get('sha256', ''))):
            raise ValueError('malformed input row: ' + str(path))
        source = (base / row['path']).resolve()
        if source in resolved or not source.is_file():
            raise ValueError('duplicate/missing indexed input: ' + str(source))
        resolved[source] = row['sha256']
    return path, resolved


def validate_current(root, problem, active, status):
    from compcert_gate import kernel_record
    root = Path(root).resolve()
    path = active / 'evidence/goal-validation.json'
    data = json.loads(path.read_text())
    if data.get('schema') != 'five-proof-validation/1':
        raise ValueError('unsupported current proof validation schema')
    def checked(row):
        if not isinstance(row, dict) or not isinstance(row.get('path'), str):
            raise ValueError('malformed current binding')
        source = (root / row['path']).resolve()
        if not source.is_relative_to(root) or not source.is_file() or digest(source) != row.get('sha256'):
            raise ValueError('stale/missing current binding: ' + str(source))
        return source
    index, historical = input_index(root, active)
    if checked(data.get('index')) != index:
        raise ValueError('wrong input index binding')
    rows = data.get('inputs')
    if not isinstance(rows, list) or not rows:
        raise ValueError('missing current input bindings')
    current, snapshots = {}, {}
    for row in rows:
        source = checked(row)
        if source in current:
            raise ValueError('duplicate current input')
        current[source] = row['sha256']
        if row.get('snapshot'):
            snapshot = (root / row['snapshot']).resolve()
            if not snapshot.is_relative_to(root) or not snapshot.is_file() or digest(snapshot) != row['sha256']:
                raise ValueError('current source differs from compiled snapshot: ' + str(source))
            if snapshot in snapshots:
                raise ValueError('ambiguous compiled snapshot')
            snapshots[snapshot] = source
    required = set(historical) | {problem / 'Spec.v', active / 'Proof.v', active / 'check.py'}
    if not required.issubset(current):
        raise ValueError('current bindings omit indexed/proof/spec/checker inputs')
    # Old manifest histories are immutable, but current executable sources must
    # still match their original index as well as their fresh compiled snapshot.
    for source, old_hash in historical.items():
        if source.suffix in ('.v', '.c') and current[source] != old_hash:
            raise ValueError('source differs from retained input index: ' + str(source))
    if not {problem / 'Spec.v', active / 'Proof.v'}.issubset(set(snapshots.values())):
        raise ValueError('current Proof/Spec missing compiled snapshots')
    receipt_ref = data['kernel_evidence']
    kernel_record(root, receipt_ref)
    receipt = json.loads((root / receipt_ref).read_text())
    dependencies = {(root / name).resolve(): value for name, value in receipt['dependency_sha256'].items()}
    if set(dependencies) != set(snapshots):
        raise ValueError('current source bindings do not cover exact kernel dependency closure')
    if any(current[snapshots[p]] != value for p, value in dependencies.items()):
        raise ValueError('kernel dependency hash differs from current source')
    proof_run = json.loads((root / receipt['run'] / 'run.json').read_text())
    def full_compile(command):
        # Reference full-build shape only: load paths, harmless output flags,
        # and exactly one source. Output/module overrides can leave stale .vo
        # files at the path later consumed by the kernel, so fail closed.
        argv = command.get('argv', [])
        if not argv or command.get('status') != 'passed' or command.get('exit_code') != 0:
            return False
        if Path(argv[0]).name == 'rocq' and argv[1:2] == ['compile']:
            args = argv[2:]
        elif Path(argv[0]).name == 'coqc':
            args = argv[1:]
        else:
            return False
        sources = 0
        i = 0
        while i < len(args):
            if args[i] in ('-Q', '-R') and i + 2 < len(args):
                i += 3
            elif args[i] == '-I' and i + 1 < len(args):
                i += 2
            elif args[i] in ('-q', '-quiet', '-time'):
                i += 1
            elif not args[i].startswith('-') and args[i].endswith('.v'):
                sources += 1
                i += 1
            else:
                return False
        return sources == 1
    compiled = set()
    for command in proof_run.get('commands', []):
        argv = command.get('argv', [])
        if full_compile(command):
            compiled.update((Path(command['cwd']) / arg).resolve() for arg in argv[1:] if arg.endswith('.v'))
    if not set(dependencies).issubset(compiled):
        raise ValueError('kernel dependency source was not compiled in the bound proof run')
    kernel_commands = [c for c in proof_run.get('commands', []) if c.get('id') == receipt['command_id']]
    def module_candidates(command, module):
        args = command['argv']; mappings = []
        for i, arg in enumerate(args):
            if arg in ('-Q', '-R') and i + 2 < len(args):
                mappings.append((args[i + 2], (Path(command['cwd']) / args[i + 1]).resolve()))
        matching = [(prefix, directory) for prefix, directory in mappings if module == prefix or module.startswith(prefix + '.')]
        if not matching:
            return []
        longest = max(len(prefix) for prefix, _ in matching)
        matching = [(prefix, directory) for prefix, directory in matching if len(prefix) == longest]
        if len(matching) != 1:
            raise ValueError('ambiguous logical namespace mapping: ' + module)
        prefix, directory = matching[0]
        return [directory.joinpath(*module[len(prefix):].strip('.').split('.')).with_suffix('.v')]
    for theorem in receipt['theorems']:
        module = theorem.rsplit('.', 1)[0]
        candidates = module_candidates(kernel_commands[0], module)
        if len(candidates) != 1 or candidates[0] not in dependencies:
            raise ValueError('kernel theorem module does not resolve to bound dependency snapshot')
        source = candidates[0]
        matching_compiles = [c for c in proof_run.get('commands', []) if full_compile(c) and any((Path(c['cwd']) / arg).resolve() == source for arg in c['argv'] if arg.endswith('.v'))]
        if not matching_compiles or any(module_candidates(c, module) != [source] for c in matching_compiles):
            raise ValueError('proof compile and kernel namespace mappings differ')
    bindings = data.get('goal_bindings')
    goals = status.get('requested_goals')
    if not isinstance(bindings, list) or not bindings or not isinstance(goals, list) or len(set(goals)) != len(goals):
        raise ValueError('missing/malformed goal bindings')
    if [r.get('requested_goal') for r in bindings] != goals:
        raise ValueError('requested goals differ from certified goals')
    ident = r'[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z_0-9]*(?:\.[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z_0-9]*)*'
    for row in bindings:
        if not re.fullmatch(ident, str(row.get('theorem', ''))) or not isinstance(row.get('type'), str) or not row['type'].strip() or any(token in row['type'] for token in ('(*', '*)', '\n', '\r')) or re.search(r'\.(?:\s|$)', row['type']):
            raise ValueError('malformed theorem/type binding')
        if row['theorem'] not in receipt['theorems']:
            raise ValueError('goal theorem is not claimed by kernel receipt')
    cert = data['certificate']
    certificate = checked(cert)
    imports = cert.get('imports')
    if not isinstance(imports, list) or not imports or not all(re.fullmatch(ident, str(n)) for n in imports):
        raise ValueError('malformed certificate imports')
    if certificate.read_text() != certificate_source(imports, bindings):
        raise ValueError('certificate does not express exact theorem-to-goal bindings')
    run = json.loads((root / cert['run'] / 'run.json').read_text())
    if run.get('status') != 'passed':
        raise ValueError('certificate run did not pass')
    run_inputs = {Path(x['source']).resolve(): x['sha256'] for x in run.get('inputs', [])}
    if run_inputs.get(certificate) != cert['sha256'] or any(run_inputs.get(p) != h for p, h in dependencies.items()):
        raise ValueError('certificate run omitted actual certificate/dependency snapshot')
    def command(command_id):
        rows = [c for c in run.get('commands', []) if c.get('id') == command_id]
        if len(rows) != 1 or rows[0].get('exit_code') != 0 or rows[0].get('status') != 'passed':
            raise ValueError('missing/failed certificate command')
        return rows[0]
    compile_row = command(cert['compile_command_id'])
    stdout = compile_row.get('stdout')
    if not isinstance(stdout, str) or not (root / cert['run'] / stdout).is_file() or not (root / cert['run'] / stdout).stat().st_size:
        raise ValueError('missing actual certificate Print Assumptions output')
    argv = compile_row['argv']
    if not full_compile(compile_row) or not any((Path(compile_row['cwd']) / arg).resolve() == certificate for arg in argv if arg.endswith('.v')):
        raise ValueError('certificate was not actually compiled')
    # Reuse canonical independent-kernel and compilation/snapshot checks for
    # certificate module, avoiding a second permissive argv implementation.
    certificate_receipt = cert['kernel_evidence']
    kernel_record(root, certificate_receipt)
    ce = json.loads((root / certificate_receipt).read_text())
    if ce['run'] != cert['run'] or ce['command_id'] != cert['kernel_command_id'] or ce['theorems'] != [cert['module'] + '.goal_' + str(i) for i in range(len(bindings))] or ce['statement_artifacts'] != [cert['path']] or ce['dependency_sha256'] != {**receipt['dependency_sha256'], cert['path']: cert['sha256']}:
        raise ValueError('certificate kernel receipt differs from exact certification')
    # Imports must resolve to the very same compiled dependency source paths.
    for row in (compile_row, command(cert['kernel_command_id'])):
        for module in set(imports) | {b['theorem'].rsplit('.', 1)[0] for b in bindings} | {b['type'].rsplit('.', 1)[0] for b in bindings if re.fullmatch(ident, b['type']) and '.' in b['type']}:
            candidates = module_candidates(row, module)
            if not any(p in dependencies for p in candidates):
                raise ValueError('certificate import not bound to actual compiled snapshot: ' + module)
        if certificate not in module_candidates(row, cert['module']):
            raise ValueError('certificate module does not resolve to actual compiled certificate')
 indexed={row["path"]:row["sha256"] for row in bindings}
 for e in ("get_first_order_low_pass","reset_first_order_low_pass"):
  c=root/"paparazzi/models"/e
  for rel in ("prepare/source/"+e+".c","prepare/source/bindings.json","align/request.json","align/model/compcert-manifest.json","align/model/preprocessed.i"):
   p=c/rel;indexed[str(p.relative_to(root))]=digest(p)
 indexed[str((attempt/"check.py").relative_to(root))]=digest(attempt/"check.py")
 dump(attempt/"provenance.json",{"schema":"five-proof-attempt-provenance/1","files":[{"path":p,"sha256":h} for p,h in sorted(indexed.items())]})
 bound={x["path"]:x for x in bindings}
 for p,h in indexed.items():bound.setdefault(p,{"path":p,"sha256":h})
 validation={"schema":"five-proof-validation/1","index":{"path":str((attempt/"provenance.json").relative_to(root)),"sha256":digest(attempt/"provenance.json")},"inputs":list(bound.values()),"kernel_evidence":str((evidence/"kernel-evidence.json").relative_to(root)),"goal_bindings":goals,"certificate":{"path":str(cert.relative_to(root)),"sha256":digest(cert),"module":"FiveLowpassGetNoError.GoalBinding","imports":["FiveLowpassGetNoError.Spec","FiveLowpassGetNoError.Proof"],"run":runpath,"compile_command_id":comp["id"],"kernel_command_id":check["id"],"kernel_evidence":str((evidence/"certificate-kernel-evidence.json").relative_to(root))}}
 dump(evidence/"goal-validation.json",validation)
 print("All exact goals compiled, assumptions emitted, independently kernel checked.")
